  "external_logs": {
    "why": "the issue asks the estimator to be run on real flight logs (PX4 Flight Review, the CMU ALFA dataset). Neither could be obtained from this machine, and no run is reported rather than a fabricated one",
    "probes": [
      {
        "url": "https://review.px4.io/",
        "http": 200,
        "what": "the service is alive"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://review.px4.io/browse",
        "http": 200,
        "what": "returns a page with no log ids: Flight Review has no public index, a log is reachable only by the id its owner publishes, and there is no id to use"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://theairlab.org/alfa-dataset/",
        "http": 200,
        "what": "ALFA: 1.7 GB zipped (12.5 GB unzipped) of ROS .bag files from an ArduPilot Pixhawk over MAVLink 2.0, behind a Box shared link"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://api.box.com/2.0/shared_items",
        "http": 401,
        "what": "an anonymous shared-link query to the Box API needs an app token"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://kilthub.cmu.edu/api/datasets/:persistentId/?persistentId=doi:10.1184/R1/12707963",
        "http": 202,
        "what": "the Dataverse record behind the DOI answers the API with an empty body (bot challenge)"
      }
    ],
    "what_a_test_would_need": [
      "time-aligned accelerometer, gyro, attitude and GPS velocity at a known rate -- ALFA's .bag and a PX4 .ulg both have them, and this estimator's interface (OnlineExpert.update) takes exactly those plus the rotor speed",
      "the rotor speed the thrust is computed from. This simulator's ESC reports it; a log carries a PWM command and not the speed, so a PWM -> omega curve has to be identified first, and that curve is the largest single error term the expert has (a 1 % speed error is a 2 % thrust error, which is the whole vertical drag signal)",
      "the mass and the inertia of the airframe the log was flown on, which neither dataset publishes per flight; without them nothing can be scored, only cross-checked",
      "an interactive download (a browser or an authenticated client) and a .bag/.ulg reader, neither of which this environment has"
    ]
  },
